shell_browser_main_parts.cc includes an Android-only header unconditionally:

    ../../content/shell/browser/shell_browser_main_parts.cc:28:10: fatal error:
    content/shell/android/shell_descriptors.h: No such file or directory

QtWebEngine's distribution ships content/shell/android/ with only BUILD.gn in
it, so the header genuinely is not there. The other three vendored Shell files
that reference the same header -- app/shell_crash_reporter_client.cc,
app/shell_main_delegate.cc, browser/shell_content_browser_client.cc -- all
guard it behind `#if defined(OS_ANDROID)` and all three compiled fine. Only
this one file has the include at top level, and it is still that way as late
as upstream 95, so it is an upstream oversight that no non-Android build
happened to trip over: nothing from the header is used anywhere in this file
(grep for shell_descriptors or any symbol it declares finds only the include
line itself; every OS_ANDROID block in the file is unrelated).

Dropping the include is therefore the honest fix, and preferable to vendoring
shell_descriptors.h under missing_sources/ for a file that would go unused.

--- a/upstream/content_shell/browser/shell_browser_main_parts.cc
+++ b/upstream/content_shell/browser/shell_browser_main_parts.cc
@@ -25,7 +25,6 @@
 #include "content/public/common/main_function_params.h"
 #include "content/public/common/result_codes.h"
 #include "content/public/common/url_constants.h"
-#include "content/shell/android/shell_descriptors.h"
 #include "content/shell/browser/shell.h"
 #include "content/shell/browser/shell_browser_context.h"
 #include "content/shell/browser/shell_devtools_manager_delegate.h"
